# Ghi công và thông báo bên thứ ba

Giữ nguyên văn các điều khoản giấy phép dưới đây. Tệp này không cấp giấy
phép mã nguồn mở cho phần mã riêng của AirDesk. Chủ dự án chưa chọn giấy
phép đó. Các phiên bản thư viện đang dùng được cố định trong pyproject.toml.
Model Google được giữ kèm văn bản Apache-2.0 tại assets/models/LICENSE.

AirDesk is original code. The components below were studied and the noted parts adapted
(re-implemented, not copied verbatim unless stated). Their licenses are reproduced as required.

| Project | Commit | License | What AirDesk uses |
|---|---|---|---|
| [AirTouch](https://github.com/Jhnbismark/airtouch) | 8bd72f3 | MIT | Adaptive Kalman idea: speed-scaled process noise in log space, speed-gated clamped prediction, constants `SPEED_LO/HI`, `PRED_LO/HI`, `q_min/q_max/r`. Re-written as two independent 2-state filters (`airdesk/core/filters.py`). |
| [AirCursor](https://github.com/FarzamFattahi/aircursor) | b44af9f | MIT | Hand-identity continuity idea (follow the same wrist across frames) in `airdesk/core/selection.py` `HandSelector`. |
| [Alpha-OSK](https://github.com/owenpkent/alpha-osk) | eb12523 | MIT | Win32 lessons for on-screen keyboards: INPUT union must contain MOUSEINPUT, KEYEVENTF_UNICODE, re-applying WS_EX_NOACTIVATE after Qt creates the HWND (`airdesk/platform/win32.py`, `airdesk/ui/keyboard_overlay.py`). |
| [1€ Filter](https://github.com/casiez/OneEuroFilter) | d789255 | BSD-3-Clause (reference code) | Algorithm from Casiez, Roussel & Vogel, CHI 2012; re-implemented from the paper in `airdesk/core/filters.py`. |
| [MediaPipe](https://github.com/google-ai-edge/mediapipe) | pip 1.1.1 | Apache-2.0 | Hand Landmarker task and model `assets/models/hand_landmarker.task`. |
| Qt for Python (PySide6) | pip 6.12.0 | LGPL-3.0 | GUI toolkit, dynamically linked (shipped as separate DLLs in the onedir build). |
| OpenCV | pip 5.0.0 | Apache-2.0 | Camera capture and image resizing. |
| NumPy, Matplotlib, Pillow | pip | BSD / PSF-style | Numerics, benchmark charts, icon generation (build time). |

Reviewed for reference only (no code or design adopted): Mouseless (MIT), handmouse (no license file - not reused),
py-hand-tracker (MIT), virtual-keyboard-and-mouse (MIT), OptiKey (GPL - reference only, nothing adopted).


